            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A method for processing hazard reports received from vehicles is provided. The method includes receiving, from a first navigation system of a first vehicle, a first report, wherein the first report was generated by the first navigation system after detecting at least a first safety hazard in an environment of the first vehicle based on an analysis of image data collected by the first navigation system, receiving, from a second navigation system of a second vehicle, a second report, wherein the second report was generated by the second navigation system after detecting at least a second safety hazard in an environment of the second vehicle based on an analysis of image data collected by the second navigation system, processing the first report and the second report to determine that the first report and the second report identify a similar hazard, in response to determining that the first and second reports identify a similar hazard, aggregating the first report and the second report into an aggregated report associated with a hazard, wherein the hazard corresponds to the similar hazard, processing the aggregated report to determine a root cause and/or a contributing factor associated with the hazard, and providing an indicator of the hazard on a map.</p>
            </abstract>
